<title>CANADA: Four Seasons to sell Toronto hotel.</title>
<headline>Four Seasons to sell Toronto hotel.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four Seasons Hotels Inc said Friday the freehold and leasehold interests in the Four Seasons Toronto Hotel will be sold to a Maritz Wolff limited partnership.</p>
<p>Four Seasons will continue to manage the Toronto hotel under a long-term agreement. The leasehold is expected to close in early January, 1997.</p>
<p>In addition to the long-term agreement, Four Seasons will receive about C$13 million at closing to be used for the reduction of corporate debt, Four Seasons said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
